<section>
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item colspan="7" background-color="accent" padding="34pt 12pt 30pt">
      <p role="eyebrow">Field guide</p>
      <spacer mode="fill"/>
      <p role="caption">TRANSITION</p>
      <p role="caption">10 / 10</p>
    </grid-item>
    <grid-item colspan="53" padding="0">
      <grid spacing="none">
        <grid-item colspan="16" padding="0">
          <ai-image prompt="Editorial studio photograph of a sequence of modular warm-white paper blocks connected across a thirty-day transition path, operational-blue cord passing through field-sage accepted gates with one signal-amber decision gate, graphite clips and translucent tabs, soft directional daylight, precise and calm, no text, lettering, people, logos, or screens" image-style="operational-still-life" aspect-ratio="portrait" fill="true"/>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="44" padding="30pt 38pt 26pt">
          <labels><label variant="outline">Illustrative replacement · validate before use</label></labels>
          <h2>The next 30 days turn transferred knowledge into accepted ownership</h2>
          <p font-size="sm">T+0 is the formal start of handover. Relative markers begin when handover is formally accepted.</p>
          <table borders="rows" striped="false" col-widths="[9,16,35]">
            <tr><th>When</th><th>Owner</th><th>Required result</th></tr>
            <tr><td background-color="accent"><p font-size="sm"><b>T+1</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Incoming PM</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Confirm owners, deputies, artifact locations, invitations, and access requests.</p></td></tr>
            <tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>T+3</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Incoming PM</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Walk the system path, reconcile the delivery board, and record contradictions.</p></td></tr>
            <tr><td background-color="palette-2"><p font-size="sm"><b>T+5</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Data + Operations</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Complete A-06 benchmark, training, and rollback rehearsal.</p></td></tr>
            <tr><td background-color="palette-2"><p font-size="sm"><b>T+6</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Product Owner</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Decide D-04 from benchmark evidence and record the consequence.</p></td></tr>
            <tr><td background-color="palette-3"><p font-size="sm"><b>T+10</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Product Owner + PM</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Review failed tests, roles, fallback, and authority; accept or extend handover.</p></td></tr>
            <tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>T+15</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Technical + Operations</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Execute the first rollout only if entry criteria are met.</p></td></tr>
            <tr><td><p font-size="sm"><b>T+30</b></p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Product Owner + PM</p></td><td><p font-size="sm">Review stability, adoption, unresolved risks, and temporary controls.</p></td></tr>
          </table>
          <aside variant="success">
            <p font-size="sm"><b>Acceptance test:</b> the incoming owner can explain the purpose, locate authoritative evidence, identify who can decide, describe rollback, and name the next three actions without help.</p>
          </aside>
          <p role="caption">Anything that still depends on private memory becomes a documented action, not an assumption.</p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>